StockBuddy is tested using a combination of manual testing and planned integration testing. Functional testing is performed to ensure that key features such as scanning items, adding products, completing transactions, and updating inventory operate correctly. Input validation and error handling are also tested to confirm the system behaves properly with invalid or unexpected data. Integration testing is planned to verify that the user interface, database operations, and business logic work together correctly during real transaction workflows. MSTest was used to perform unit tests on checkout processes.
